+# Tool Input Validation
+
+| Field  | Value                |
+| ------ | -------------------- |
+| Issue  | re-cinq/HALEngine#37 |
+| Status | Draft                |
+
+The registry validates each tool call against the same JSON Schema given to providers, so a model can correct a malformed call within the existing tool-round limit.
+
+## Registry contract
+
+- Before invoking a tool executor, `ToolRegistry.execute` rejects missing required properties, wrong types, and disallowed enum members with a `ToolResponse.result` naming the property path and constraint, without including the supplied value or passing the input to the executor. ([validated by: rejects missing, wrong-typed and disallowed input before execution without revealing values](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L16))
+- Input accepted by the registered schema reaches the executor unchanged, including unlisted properties, and is executed exactly once; validation does not coerce values, apply defaults, or forbid extra properties by default. ([validated by: passes schema-valid input with unlisted properties through unchanged exactly once](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L47))
+- A static tool's schema is compiled at registration, so an invalid schema throws then with the tool name, and subsequent executions use the compiled schema. ([validated by: rejects an invalid static schema at registration and keeps a compiled static schema for later calls](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L63))
+- A function-valued tool definition resolves for each call and validates against the schema current at that call, with compiled schemas cached by resolved schema object. ([validated by: validates each call against the current function-valued definition](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L81))
+- An unregistered tool name still throws `Unknown tool: <name>`. ([validated by: rejects missing, wrong-typed and disallowed input before execution without revealing values](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L16))
+
+## Conversation contract
+
+- A schema rejection is a tool result rather than an exception: the orchestrator returns it to the provider on the next round, allowing a corrected call to finish within the configured maximum tool rounds. ([validated by: returns a schema rejection to the provider so a corrected tool call can finish the conversation](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.acceptance.test.ts#L7))
